--- Returns an arrow that calls `f` with its first two arguments swapped.
---
--- @details
--- `flip` adapts a two-argument function to the opposite argument
--- order. It is most useful for feeding a non-commutative function
--- into a pipeline or fold that supplies arguments in a fixed order.
---
--- Only the first two arguments are swapped; the result takes
--- exactly two arguments.
---
--- @example
--- `sub :: [a, b] ~> a - b`
--- `[10, 3] >>> (sub >>> comb.flip) >>> comb.apply`
--- -- => -7
---
export flip :: f ~> x ~> y ~> f(y, x)
